{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:AppendixStandardModel.GaugeActionGroupoid","@type":"LeanModule","name":"AppendixStandardModel.GaugeActionGroupoid","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Groupoid","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Endomorphism","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Submonoid.Basic"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.GaugeActionGroupoid.zeroActionEnd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.GaugeActionGroupoid.zeroActionEnd","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-standard-model/gauge-action-groupoid.lean#L88-L97","doc":"The automorphisms of a fixed state with zero action form a\nsubmonoid of `End X`: the **residual (unbroken) symmetries** of that\nstate. Closure is additivity of the action; the identity is free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.GaugeActionGroupoid.gaugeEquiv_equivalence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.GaugeActionGroupoid.gaugeEquiv_equivalence","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-standard-model/gauge-action-groupoid.lean#L80-L86","doc":"Gauge equivalence is an equivalence relation — reflexive via the\nidentity, symmetric via groupoid inversion, transitive via\ncomposition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.GaugeActionGroupoid.GaugeEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.GaugeActionGroupoid.GaugeEquiv","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-standard-model/gauge-action-groupoid.lean#L76-L78","doc":"**Gauge equivalence**: two states are gauge equivalent when some\ngauge transformation connects them. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.GaugeActionGroupoid.act_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.GaugeActionGroupoid.act_inv","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-standard-model/gauge-action-groupoid.lean#L67-L74","doc":"Undoing a gauge transformation refunds its action: a closed\ngauge loop `f ≫ f⁻¹` costs zero, so `act f⁻¹ = -act f`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.GaugeActionGroupoid.act_comp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.GaugeActionGroupoid.act_comp","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-standard-model/gauge-action-groupoid.lean#L58-L58","doc":"The action is additive under composition of deformations. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.GaugeActionGroupoid.act_id","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.GaugeActionGroupoid.act_id","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-standard-model/gauge-action-groupoid.lean#L56-L56","doc":"Doing nothing costs nothing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.GaugeActionGroupoid.act","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.GaugeActionGroupoid.act","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-standard-model/gauge-action-groupoid.lean#L54-L54","doc":"The action cost of a gauge transformation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.GaugeActionGroupoid.grpd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.GaugeActionGroupoid.grpd","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-standard-model/gauge-action-groupoid.lean#L52-L52","doc":"Gauge transformations form a groupoid: every deformation is reversible. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.GaugeActionGroupoid.states","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.GaugeActionGroupoid.states","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-standard-model/gauge-action-groupoid.lean#L50-L50","doc":"The topological states (objects: knot / braid configurations). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.GaugeActionGroupoid.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.GaugeActionGroupoid.mk","kind":"ctor","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-standard-model/gauge-action-groupoid.lean#L48-L48","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.GaugeActionGroupoid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.GaugeActionGroupoid","kind":"structure","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-standard-model/gauge-action-groupoid.lean#L42-L59","doc":"A **gauge action groupoid** over an additive commutative group\n`R` of action values: a groupoid of topological states whose\nmorphisms (gauge transformations) carry an action functional `act`\nthat vanishes on identities and is additive under composition.\nReversibility of gauge transformations is exactly the groupoid\naxiom. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:gauge-action-groupoid","label":"def:gauge-action-groupoid","md":"quantum-observable-universe/appendix-standard-model/gauge-action-groupoid.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}